ll due to saturated\nsoils and increased runoff potential. Thus, prolonged periods of\nadditional rainfall over these regions would trigger a similar\nresponse. The current precipitation forecast suggests larger peaks in\nseveral creeks and rivers than what has been observed over the\nprevious 7 days. However, high end probabilistic rainfall amounts\n(i.e. above 90th percentile) may lead to rivers exceeding action\nstage to minor flooding. Most probable basins to see significant\nrises include; the Rio Blanco, San Juan, Piedra, Los Pinos/Vallecito\nCreek, and the Animas River Basins.\n\nConvective storms and periods of heavy rainfall fed from said\ntropical moisture could result in localized flooding impacts across\nthe CWA, however, confidence decreases rapidly north of the San\nJuans. Please continue to monitor the forecast as these systems\nevolve. Especially for those who reside and/or plan to recreate in\nthe southwest quadrant of the forecast area.","ends":"2026-09-30T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Dolores, CO; Gunnison, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Montezuma, CO; Ouray, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce67801ec73048f07c44dd0418c6a50edd1c8fdc.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce67801ec73048f07c44dd0418c6a50edd1c8fdc.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-25T20:38:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 252038 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 238 PM MDT Fri Sep 25 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Periods of moderate to occasionally heavy rain and thunderstorms will impact western Colorado and eastern Utah today. - Warmer and drier conditions return for the weekend. - Another push of moisture will arrive by Monday, bringing widespread moderate to he","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-25T18:43:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Scattered showers and thunderstorms will be around this afternoon, especially along and south of I-70. Most of eastern Utah and northwest Colorado will remain on the drier side of things. Saturday and Sunday will be mostly dry with a return to unsettled weather next week. Fire weather concerns remain low at this time. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDE","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"mnc01","station_name":"Mancos","distance_km":18.6,"soil_temp_5cm_f":67.17,"soil_temp_15cm_f":62.58,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":252.33,"wind_speed_mph":4.91,"air_temp_f":65.03,"relative_humidity":0.453,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/mnc01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KCEZ","distance_km":19.9,"raw_metar":"METAR KCEZ 252153Z AUTO 00000KT 10SM VCTS FEW049 BKN070 OVC120 21/09 A3016 RMK AO2 SLP149 T02110089","temp_f":70,"wind_dir":0,"wind_kt":0,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"OVC","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1021.4,"observed":1790373180,"raw_taf":null,"url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KCEZ&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":{"aqi":40,"category":"Good","parameter":"O3","reporting_area":"Mesa Verde National Park","observed":"2026-09-25 15","by_parameter":{"O3":{"aqi":40,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Mesa Verde National Park","observed":"2026-09-25 15"}},"url":"https://www.airnow.gov/","distance_km":5.7},"openmeteo_aq":{"pm25":2.6,"pm10":2.8,"co":111,"no2":0.6,"so2":0.3,"o3":98,"european_aqi":39,"us_aqi":43,"time":"2026-09-25T16:00"},"usgs":{"station_id":"09371492","station_name":"MUD CREEK AT STATE HIGHWAY 32, NEAR CORTEZ, CO.","distance_km":22.6,"discharge_cfs":28.1,"gauge_height_ft":2.26,"water_temp_f":60,"observed":"2026-09-25T15:30:00.000-06:00","url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/nwis/uv?site_